# Three-body recombination cross section for O + O + M --> O2 + M.
#
# sigma_rec is a cross section per unit third-body number density, so
# its units are m^5 and <sigma_rec*g> is the three-body rate
# coefficient in m^6/s.
#
# A constant value is used here so the resulting rate is exactly
# predictable and the example can be checked against theory:
#
#   reactions per volume per time = 1/2 n_O^2 n_M K <g>
#
# with <g> = sqrt(8kT/pi mr) the mean relative speed.  A real
# recombination cross section would fall off with energy; tabulate it
# here in exactly the same way.

O2_RECOMB
N 2 X energy XUNITS eV YUNITS m^5 EXTRAP constant constant

1      1.0e-6   5e-43
2      1.0e+4   5e-43
